"prose": [
{
"from": 156,
"to": 156,
"text": "The gates run on this Windows host during /implement. There is no live leg; the standing smoke is the harness cleanup → boot → status → logs → cleanup."
},
{
"from": 158,
"to": 161,
"text": "Linux-only halves have their witness in CI on the pushed sha: - the fuzz replay; - the ubuntu kill of `file_mode`'s mutants; - the Linux/macOS coverage floors."
},
{
"from": 163,
"to": 163,
"text": "The operator entries at the end read that witness."
},
{
"from": 165,
"to": 165,
"text": "Every output path the entries write is gitignored (`git check-ignore -q`, run bare at P5): `target/…`, `mutants.out`. The exception is `fuzz/target/`, which step 9 adds to `.gitignore` before the fuzz build entry first runs."
},
{
"from": 167,
"to": 167,
"text": "The local mutation entry uses `--leg`. By construction, its single-leg union cannot kill a mutant that is equivalent or compiled out on Windows: `file_mode -> None` is equivalent here, because Windows has no mode. So its `gate` read is report-only, with a stated forecast. The CI two-leg union is the verdict."
}
],
